# ANV-0052 -- a range merged away while owing a child its data
# r5 split off r7 [acct0010,acct0015) and held the only copy in pending_split_;
# r5 was then subsumed by a merge into r3, and the payload went with it
seed        = 19
workload    = shard_kv
nodes       = 5
faults      = drawn from seed; requires a merge to land inside the window
              between a split trigger applying and the child collecting
invariant   = conservation (audit), surfaced as "the cluster holds 19 accounts"
reproduce   = anvil_shard_faults 20
note        = only reachable once ANV-0051 was fixed: the seed had been halting
              at tick 4395 on a false INV-SHARD-CLIENT positive and never ran
              far enough to reach this. Fixed by making pending_split_ a map
              keyed by child id and carrying the entries in encode_span(), so a
              merge hands the debt to the survivor. Blocking the merge instead
              livelocks -- the child cannot initialise, so the split never
              confirms, so the merge never unblocks.
